WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.080 --> 00:03.280
If you walk away, don’t ever come back again, you brat!

3
00:03.720 --> 00:06.320
You stop seeing that boy right now!

4
00:06.840 --> 00:10.400
(Seeing their family fight because Bay and I are together,)

5
00:11.000 --> 00:14.000
I can’t help but feel guilty, Pa.

6
00:14.440 --> 00:16.000
Just staying by my side

7
00:16.560 --> 00:18.320
(and being cute like this is enough.)

8
00:18.360 --> 00:22.040
I already know the truth about our family stealing Chun’s dim sum recipe.

9
00:22.160 --> 00:23.720
(None of us did anything wrong.)

10
00:24.200 --> 00:26.360
(I didn’t take Chun’s recipe)

11
00:26.440 --> 00:28.120
(and you don’t have to feel guilty.)

12
00:28.120 --> 00:29.000
Bee!

13
00:33.320 --> 00:34.840
INCOMING CALL

14
00:41.120 --> 00:42.160
Hello, mom.

15
00:42.320 --> 00:46.400
(Bay, are you with your dad? I don’t know where he went.)

16
00:48.960 --> 00:49.360
Mom.

17
00:49.880 --> 00:50.920
Did you find Dad?

18
00:50.920 --> 00:51.640
I couldn’t find him.

19
00:51.640 --> 00:53.360
-Urg, where is he? -You couldn’t find him, either?

20
00:53.520 --> 00:55.280
Obviously. And he’s not picking up his phone.

21
01:12.000 --> 01:15.000
SUPPORTED BY THE DEPARTMENT OF CULTURAL PROMOTION, MINISTRY OF CULTURE

22
02:30.600 --> 02:31.400
I can’t eat anymore.

23
02:31.400 --> 02:32.640
Woman Let’s pack it home then.

24
02:39.360 --> 02:41.280
Italy, yay!

25
02:53.080 --> 02:53.720
Let’s go.

26
03:00.160 --> 03:01.040
Food waste.

27
03:06.800 --> 03:07.840
What are you looking at, uncle?!

28
03:10.400 --> 03:11.760
What’s up, son?!

29
03:12.240 --> 03:14.960
I didn’t know I was your dad’s brother.

30
03:15.000 --> 03:16.200
Watch your mouth, old man.

31
03:16.280 --> 03:19.640
Scumbag! I’m not all talk.

32
03:19.880 --> 03:21.520
You don’t wanna mess with me…

33
03:22.000 --> 03:23.960
Son of a b*tch!

34
03:24.240 --> 03:26.200
Sh*t! Why did you punch me?!

35
03:26.400 --> 03:27.160
How about that, uncle?

36
03:27.160 --> 03:28.720
How about this?!

37
03:32.160 --> 03:32.760
Easy!

38
03:38.760 --> 03:39.360
Hey!

39
03:46.600 --> 03:47.360
Hey! Bay!

40
03:47.440 --> 03:48.000
No!

41
03:50.880 --> 03:54.120
Now hold on! Are you trying to murder him?!

42
03:54.280 --> 03:54.920
Easy!

43
03:56.560 --> 03:59.320
-Officer! Officer! Officer! -Officer! Officer!

44
03:59.320 --> 04:00.760
-Let’s go! -There’s a fight over here!

45
04:00.760 --> 04:01.480
Get lost!

46
04:03.080 --> 04:04.120
-Bay! -Bay!

47
04:05.320 --> 04:06.280
Are you alright?

48
04:13.960 --> 04:15.760
Why did you pick a fight with those guys?

49
04:16.000 --> 04:18.920
You’re lucky we got there in time!

50
04:22.920 --> 04:23.440
Bay.

51
04:25.480 --> 04:27.520
I think we all should get some rest, son.

52
04:28.800 --> 04:31.200
We can’t solve anything until everyone’s calmed down.

53
04:35.720 --> 04:37.080
You’re his Pa now?

54
04:38.720 --> 04:40.440
His damn Pa?

55
04:41.320 --> 04:44.360
Great. Take everything from me.

56
04:44.840 --> 04:46.760
Can you stop being a jerk?

57
04:47.000 --> 04:49.320
No one has the energy to fight with you anymore.

58
04:49.360 --> 04:53.800
Why don’t you stop babbling and get out of my face?

59
04:55.240 --> 04:56.480
You need to stop.

60
04:57.320 --> 04:59.960
Everyone risked their lives to save you today.

61
05:00.000 --> 05:01.000
Don’t you have any gratitude?

62
05:01.720 --> 05:05.200
You’re acting crazy and trying to control everyone

63
05:06.080 --> 05:08.520
because you want to justify yourself, right?

64
05:08.920 --> 05:14.240
That you weren’t wrong when you chose to betray Chun back then.

65
05:14.560 --> 05:15.480
Am I right?

66
05:26.640 --> 05:28.640
I’m sorry, Chun.

67
05:31.600 --> 05:33.400
I’m sorry, kids.

68
05:34.320 --> 05:35.800
I knew everything.

69
05:37.160 --> 05:40.000
But I never tried to make it right.

70
05:48.880 --> 05:50.680
If you want any compensation,

71
05:51.280 --> 05:53.080
we’ll take responsibility for it.

72
06:10.920 --> 06:12.680
If you call it quits, I’ll do the same.

73
06:14.080 --> 06:15.720
I don’t want to take anything from you.

74
06:17.360 --> 06:20.880
I only want you to leave me and my son alone. That’s all.

75
06:32.280 --> 06:34.200
Tell Chun you’re sorry.

76
06:34.840 --> 06:38.000
And just let Bay and Boat be.

77
06:42.080 --> 06:42.840
Or else…

78
06:45.560 --> 06:47.320
our marriage is over.

79
06:50.680 --> 06:51.640
Honey…

80
06:53.160 --> 06:55.480
Do you have to go that far?

81
06:56.800 --> 06:57.600
Damn it.

82
07:01.120 --> 07:02.360
I’ll go live with Mom.

83
07:10.800 --> 07:11.280
Me, too.

84
07:15.480 --> 07:16.920
What are you guys talking about?

85
07:17.920 --> 07:21.800
Do you hate your dad that much? Huh?

86
07:22.880 --> 07:23.600
Boat.

87
07:27.640 --> 07:28.360
Honey.

88
07:32.240 --> 07:37.080
You’re luckier than me that you still have a chance.

89
08:05.880 --> 08:07.360
I’m sorry, Chun

90
08:10.880 --> 08:11.800
I’m sorry.

91
08:25.040 --> 08:25.560
Bay,

92
08:28.800 --> 08:29.880
I’m sorry, son.

93
08:31.520 --> 08:32.920
I’m sorry, Boat

94
08:36.720 --> 08:37.840
I’m sorry, honey.

95
08:38.720 --> 08:39.560
I’m sorry.

96
08:40.960 --> 08:41.800
I’m sorry.

97
08:48.280 --> 08:49.040
I’m sorry.

98
08:56.840 --> 08:57.840
I’m sorry.

99
08:59.320 --> 09:00.360
I really am.

100
09:05.440 --> 09:07.240
This looks worse than I thought.

101
09:11.400 --> 09:13.040
Are you sure you’re okay?

102
09:17.720 --> 09:18.840
I’m okay.

103
09:20.040 --> 09:21.040
Don’t worry about me.

104
09:22.880 --> 09:24.960
You should go to sleep.

105
09:26.920 --> 09:28.320
I don’t think I can.

106
09:30.800 --> 09:31.960
Fortunately,

107
09:33.440 --> 09:35.080
the tryout is in the evening.

108
09:42.000 --> 09:42.960
Come get some sleep.

109
10:11.320 --> 10:15.200
I can’t wait to fall asleep and wake up tomorrow.

110
10:16.400 --> 10:17.160
Why?

111
10:18.200 --> 10:20.200
Tomorrow, you’ll get to be in the national team.

112
10:22.800 --> 10:25.280
And you and I will finally get to be together.

113
10:27.600 --> 10:29.600
I’ve been waiting for this for so long, Son.

114
10:32.400 --> 10:32.960
You…

115
10:35.200 --> 10:36.840
don’t think there’s a chance I won’t make it?

116
10:36.920 --> 10:37.640
No.

117
10:39.880 --> 10:41.240
I always know you can do it.

118
10:41.960 --> 10:43.440
I knew since we were eight.

119
10:50.440 --> 10:51.280
Good night.

120
10:52.080 --> 10:52.880
Good night

121
11:31.720 --> 11:34.960
-Can I sleep on your pillow? -Come on.

122
11:49.640 --> 11:59.400
CLOSED FOR ONE DAY. GONE TO SUPPORT MY SON

123
11:59.400 --> 12:01.760
BUSINESS CLOSED

124
12:03.080 --> 12:04.440
What are you smiling about, Chun?

125
12:04.960 --> 12:06.520
I’m just closing for renovations.

126
12:06.520 --> 12:08.680
I’ll reopen with an even better shop.

127
12:09.280 --> 12:13.520
Now that you’re fixing your shop, why don’t you fix your attitude as well?

128
12:13.800 --> 12:14.520
Fine.

129
12:15.040 --> 12:17.160
I’ll be back with a brand-new attitude.

130
12:17.240 --> 12:19.920
I’ll come up with an idea for my new shop.

131
12:20.000 --> 12:22.000
I guarantee my business will kick your business’s ass.

132
12:22.120 --> 12:24.120
It’ll be so good you’ll have to close your place down.

133
12:24.160 --> 12:26.600
Why don’t you change the recipe for your dim sum, too?

134
12:26.680 --> 12:29.520
You’ve been selling the same damn thing for a century.

135
12:30.040 --> 12:30.600
Ptui!

136
12:34.800 --> 12:36.560
TENNIS NATIONAL TEAM TRYOUT COMPETITION

137
12:48.080 --> 12:50.240
You’ll start playing after the first match is over.

138
12:50.360 --> 12:53.200
It should be around 7 PM. Please warm up beforehand.

139
12:53.760 --> 12:54.840
-Okay. -Yes.

140
13:18.080 --> 13:18.600
Bay!

141
13:21.600 --> 13:22.240
Bay!

142
13:22.920 --> 13:23.600
Bay!

143
13:24.480 --> 13:25.160
Bay!

144
13:26.520 --> 13:26.960
Bay!

145
13:28.120 --> 13:28.560
Bay!

146
13:37.880 --> 13:40.200
(Based on what you’ve told me and the ECG results,)

147
13:40.480 --> 13:43.800
it may have been caused by a severe blow to the chest from a hard object,

148
13:44.080 --> 13:46.960
which caused his heart rhythm to become irregular.

149
13:47.440 --> 13:49.680
For now, I’ve given him medication intravenously.

150
13:50.040 --> 13:51.040
If you’ll excuse me.

151
13:51.400 --> 13:52.240
Thank you.

152
14:04.280 --> 14:05.680
I don’t think I can do this, Coach.

153
14:05.800 --> 14:08.680
Sun, take a deep breath.

154
14:09.840 --> 14:11.400
How can I focus while playing?

155
14:13.640 --> 14:14.680
The match is about to start.

156
14:15.440 --> 14:16.720
You have to believe you can do it.

157
14:18.960 --> 14:19.480
Sun.

158
14:23.640 --> 14:28.560
If Bay found out he was the reason you missed your chance, it would destroy him.

159
14:32.320 --> 14:33.560
Sun, can you keep fighting?

160
14:35.560 --> 14:37.600
Can you please do this for Bay?

161
15:05.560 --> 15:06.520
Come on, Sun.

162
15:06.840 --> 15:07.920
Sun, let’s go.

163
15:07.920 --> 15:08.960
You’ve got this, Sun.

164
15:14.880 --> 15:17.480
Damn, why does it have to be today?

165
15:18.400 --> 15:21.200
Sun needs to win 2 more sets to get into the national team.

166
15:21.680 --> 15:23.600
The opponent has scored really well.

167
15:24.680 --> 15:25.880
Will Sun be able to do this?

168
15:27.320 --> 15:28.640
If he wants to play professionally,

169
15:29.360 --> 15:32.360
he has to do it, even if he has to play through his tears.

170
15:33.360 --> 15:34.120
Ready?

171
15:36.160 --> 15:37.280
Are you okay?

172
15:40.480 --> 15:41.320
I’m ready.

173
15:41.800 --> 15:43.000
Let’s begin then.

174
16:01.800 --> 16:02.400
Hey.

175
16:03.600 --> 16:04.640
It’s okay, son.

176
16:04.720 --> 16:06.000
Come back. Come back.

177
16:11.480 --> 16:12.760
It’s alright. You’re still good.

178
16:33.800 --> 16:35.000
It’s okay, son. It’s okay.

179
16:35.800 --> 16:39.920
Sun, Bay is in good hands.

180
16:40.240 --> 16:40.960
Don’t worry.

181
16:42.600 --> 16:45.440
I want you to focus only on this match, okay?

182
16:46.200 --> 16:48.000
I know it’s hard

183
16:48.840 --> 16:52.160
but I believe you can do this.

184
16:54.640 --> 16:55.280
Go, Sun.

185
16:57.200 --> 16:58.880
Sun, you’ve got this. Come on.

186
17:23.360 --> 17:23.880
(Sun.)

187
17:25.840 --> 17:28.320
If our dads still try to keep us apart like this,

188
17:29.200 --> 17:30.800
when you’re competing in the national tryout,

189
17:31.560 --> 17:33.080
I won’t be able to be there for you.

190
17:34.520 --> 17:35.200
It’s okay.

191
17:36.400 --> 17:37.240
Really?

192
17:39.520 --> 17:40.160
Really.

193
17:41.160 --> 17:42.520
Damn.

194
17:43.400 --> 17:45.440
It’s not important if I’m there or not?

195
17:46.480 --> 17:47.480
Of course, it is.

196
17:48.640 --> 17:51.360
But there will be times when you can’t be there to cheer me on, right?

197
17:52.480 --> 17:54.720
Like when you’re studying abroad.

198
18:00.240 --> 18:02.280
If I held this against you,

199
18:02.880 --> 18:04.520
how could we go on as a couple?

200
18:09.440 --> 18:13.120
But I want you to know I’ll be cheering for you,

201
18:15.560 --> 18:18.360
thinking about how well you’re playing,

202
18:19.280 --> 18:22.480
concerning if you’re ahead or behind.

203
18:23.280 --> 18:24.920
Just like when we played together.

204
18:27.240 --> 18:27.960
I know.

205
18:29.000 --> 18:33.840
Ugh, I still want to be there to cheer for you.

206
18:38.640 --> 18:39.560
How about this?

207
18:41.040 --> 18:43.960
I’ll keep playing tennis for a long time.

208
18:44.440 --> 18:46.960
Until the day you come back to cheer me on in person.

209
18:48.560 --> 18:49.120
Okay?

210
18:51.200 --> 18:54.320
Okay, I’ll hurry back so I can cheer you on.

211
18:57.880 --> 19:01.520
While I’m not there, just know I’m trying my best to come back for you.

212
19:01.800 --> 19:07.240
♪ It’s time that we fall in love ♪

213
19:07.400 --> 19:12.760
♪ It’s finally time for you and me to be in love ♪

214
19:13.040 --> 19:15.920
♪ This very second belongs to you alone ♪

215
19:15.920 --> 19:18.920
♪ My heartbeat says it's yours to own ♪

216
19:23.800 --> 19:24.560
Let’s go, Sun.

217
19:42.840 --> 19:44.360
-Yay! -That’s it!

218
19:54.960 --> 19:56.040
-Yes! -Woo!

219
19:56.080 --> 19:58.000
Sun is back.

220
19:59.400 --> 20:00.360
Good job, son. Let’s go.

221
20:09.360 --> 20:10.680
-Yeah! -Yes!

222
20:10.760 --> 20:13.040
-Nice job -Nice job

223
20:13.080 --> 20:13.760
Nice job, Sun.

224
20:14.680 --> 20:15.320
Good job.

225
20:38.720 --> 20:39.920
-Go. -Let’s go.

226
20:40.040 --> 20:40.760
Almost there, Sun.

227
20:41.120 --> 20:41.920
Give it your best shot.

228
20:42.160 --> 20:43.440
Focus, Sun, focus.

229
20:54.560 --> 20:58.040
(While I’m not there, just know I’m trying my best to come back for you.)

230
21:20.080 --> 21:21.160
Yay!

231
21:21.160 --> 21:21.680
Yes!

232
21:26.920 --> 21:29.320
Yay!

233
21:29.640 --> 21:30.400
Fantastic!

234
21:30.760 --> 21:33.000
It’s Match point, son. Hang in there.

235
21:33.040 --> 21:34.720
Just one more, Sun. One more.

236
21:35.080 --> 21:36.360
Almost there.

237
21:36.360 --> 21:37.280
Come on, Sun.

238
21:58.520 --> 21:59.880
Yay!!

239
21:59.880 --> 22:02.280
Yay!

240
22:02.280 --> 22:03.680
Yay!

241
22:10.640 --> 22:11.320
Amazing!

242
22:11.320 --> 22:12.120
Great job!

243
22:13.520 --> 22:15.040
-Well done! -Amazing!

244
22:15.040 --> 22:15.560
Sun!

245
22:16.480 --> 22:17.440
Bay’s awake.

246
22:18.760 --> 22:20.080
-What? Really? -Bay’s awake.

247
22:23.120 --> 22:27.080
-(Yay!) -(Woo!)

248
22:29.520 --> 22:30.280
Bay!

249
22:38.200 --> 22:40.760
You really did it. Nice job.

250
22:50.280 --> 22:51.640
You’re not hurt anymore?

251
22:52.480 --> 22:53.960
Mmm, I’m okay now.

252
22:58.320 --> 22:59.360
You sure?

253
23:07.240 --> 23:08.760
Don’t do this to me again.

254
23:10.600 --> 23:11.880
I don’t want to, either.

255
23:12.920 --> 23:14.680
I feel so bad.

256
23:15.240 --> 23:16.680
I didn’t get to watch you play.

257
23:17.720 --> 23:18.760
Don’t worry about it.

258
23:20.280 --> 23:21.920
You had to recover.

259
23:23.040 --> 23:24.360
But I’ve seen you on the phone.

260
23:24.560 --> 23:25.680
You did great.

261
23:27.480 --> 23:30.200
-Promise? -I promise. I promise.

262
23:39.080 --> 23:42.400
Congratulations to all students graduating today.

263
23:42.480 --> 23:45.720
From now on, you get to follow the path you chose for yourselves.

264
23:46.120 --> 23:47.760
But l’d like you to know

265
23:47.760 --> 23:48.960
CALCULUS, MY TOFU I’m always here to support you.

266
23:48.960 --> 23:50.640
I’m always here to support you.

267
23:51.560 --> 23:53.240
I wish you all good luck.

268
23:56.920 --> 23:59.400
Hey, I got into the Faculty of Fine Arts.

269
23:59.520 --> 24:02.120
-Wait. Are you serious? -Yeah.

270
24:02.120 --> 24:04.040
-Damn. I’m happy for you. -Thanks, buddy.

271
24:04.040 --> 24:04.760
So cool.

272
24:05.760 --> 24:08.000
And what about you going to Italy?

273
24:19.880 --> 24:21.280
Why did you take me here?

274
24:22.800 --> 24:26.720
Since we’ve gone public, we barely came here anymore.

275
24:32.320 --> 24:33.560
I have something to tell you.

276
24:55.000 --> 24:56.360
I got accepted by a school in Italy.

277
24:59.960 --> 25:01.440
And what did your parents say?

278
25:04.600 --> 25:05.560
I’ve talked to them

279
25:11.520 --> 25:12.320
and they said yes.

280
25:14.720 --> 25:15.720
They did?!

281
25:16.200 --> 25:17.920
You’ll really get to study abroad?

282
25:22.000 --> 25:23.280
And you’re really okay with that?

283
25:26.160 --> 25:30.240
-If you’re not, I can go to a university here… -You have to go.

284
25:32.200 --> 25:33.400
You have to.

285
25:36.920 --> 25:38.280
You’re not sad at all?

286
25:42.800 --> 25:44.440
You seem more excited than I am.

287
25:49.080 --> 25:50.680
What’s there to be sad about?

288
25:52.680 --> 25:54.920
You go do what you love over there.

289
25:55.640 --> 25:58.800
And I’ll do what I love over here.

290
26:00.160 --> 26:03.320
When the time comes, we’ll get to be together again.

291
26:03.880 --> 26:04.640
That’s all.

292
26:06.440 --> 26:08.040
And you’re not afraid we’re gonna break up?

293
26:11.960 --> 26:12.960
We don’t have to.

294
26:14.560 --> 26:18.400
Didn’t you say it yourself that even though we weren’t together,

295
26:19.640 --> 26:21.560
you’d still be cheering me on from there.

296
26:23.800 --> 26:25.240
A good love

297
26:26.840 --> 26:28.440
should be pushing you forward

298
26:29.480 --> 26:30.840
not holding you back.

299
26:34.080 --> 26:38.440
And…I’ll be supporting you from here, too.

300
26:41.800 --> 26:43.200
You are so adorable.

301
26:43.960 --> 26:45.360
You should adore me then.

302
26:46.160 --> 26:47.840
I adore you.

303
26:48.480 --> 26:50.720
Who wouldn’t love you, my little tofu?

304
26:52.920 --> 26:55.360
We should’ve started dating when we were eight

305
26:55.640 --> 26:57.840
so we had more time together before I leave.

306
26:58.560 --> 26:59.680
Are you crazy?

307
27:01.200 --> 27:02.440
You’re so silly.

308
27:04.520 --> 27:05.200
Woo!

309
27:16.560 --> 27:18.040
-Let’s share. -What’d you wanna eat?

310
27:18.080 --> 27:18.800
Want some?

311
27:18.800 --> 27:20.040
-You want it? -Want some?

312
27:20.040 --> 27:21.920
-Here comes the pizza. -No, I’m good.

313
27:22.200 --> 27:25.000
-Here’s the pizza. -Thank you.

314
27:25.160 --> 27:26.960
-Come on. -Here we go.

315
27:27.040 --> 27:28.360
-Share it. -I’ll go first.

316
27:28.360 --> 27:30.280
That table, take this.

317
27:31.960 --> 27:34.120
Hey, Bay, can you speak Italian?

318
27:34.760 --> 27:37.400
-Of course, bonjour. -Bonjour my ass.

319
27:37.400 --> 27:41.800
You jerk. I’ll poke you with a fork. Watch it.

320
27:41.800 --> 27:43.040
There’s only one slide left?

321
27:43.560 --> 27:44.120
Yeah.

322
27:44.600 --> 27:48.520
-Where’s mine? -You’ll be in Italy. You can eat pizza every day.

323
27:48.520 --> 27:51.840
-What the hell? I wanna eat it. -Do you want mine?

324
27:51.920 --> 27:52.480
Hey.

325
27:53.520 --> 27:55.480
I’m okay. You eat it, babe.

326
27:55.480 --> 27:58.480
What’s with the baby voice?

327
27:58.480 --> 28:01.040
-“You eat it, babe”, he said. -What are you talking about?

328
28:01.040 --> 28:05.080
-You’ve never sweet talked to me like that. -Why? You’re not my boyfriend.

329
28:05.120 --> 28:06.000
Or do you want to be?

330
28:08.520 --> 28:09.840
I’m just kidding.

331
28:10.360 --> 28:12.440
I’ll take the left-over home.

332
28:12.560 --> 28:14.200
What are you whispering about?

333
28:14.840 --> 28:15.920
I brought you pizza.

334
28:16.120 --> 28:20.200
I didn’t have to, Boat. We got plenty of food here.

335
28:20.640 --> 28:21.880
Boat loves his pizza.

336
28:22.600 --> 28:25.720
He has tried all the pizza around the country.

337
28:25.960 --> 28:28.560
He wanted to eat some today so he ordered it. Right?

338
28:28.680 --> 28:30.880
-You know me, Dad. -I sure do.

339
28:31.360 --> 28:33.000
If your son loves pizza that much,

340
28:33.000 --> 28:34.840
why don’t you open a pizza shop?

341
28:40.480 --> 28:42.680
-You two, enjoy. I’ll be outside -Okay

342
28:46.600 --> 28:48.160
Is this edible?

343
28:53.240 --> 28:54.400
Wanna try some?

344
28:54.400 --> 28:58.000
If it’s not good, I’ll let you kick me in the face.

345
28:58.080 --> 29:01.680
Can I kick you first and then I’ll try it?

346
29:01.880 --> 29:02.880
Look at you.

347
29:05.040 --> 29:06.360
This is life changing.

348
29:06.840 --> 29:08.560
You go girl.

349
29:09.600 --> 29:11.120
Go, go, go.

350
29:13.720 --> 29:14.400
Yay!

351
29:16.480 --> 29:18.440
You’re making me blush.

352
29:31.640 --> 29:33.360
Have the kids been drinking?

353
29:33.480 --> 29:35.280
It’s just their personality.

354
29:35.800 --> 29:38.440
They’ve had a whole box of soda.

355
29:38.640 --> 29:40.040
I think they’re drunk on sugar.

356
29:41.320 --> 29:42.880
Will I ever get to see you two again?

357
29:43.360 --> 29:45.200
You’ll be studying abroad.

358
29:45.440 --> 29:47.000
And you’ll be with the national team.

359
29:47.120 --> 29:48.440
You’ll forget about me.

360
29:49.040 --> 29:51.440
No way. How can I forget you?

361
29:51.480 --> 29:53.120
-Really. -Really.

362
29:53.280 --> 29:57.960
You’ll see. I’ll be the best club leader.

363
29:58.120 --> 30:00.000
And I will be the next PREM’S GAME champion.

364
30:00.000 --> 30:03.560
Because I was there during your era and I got to play with you.

365
30:03.600 --> 30:05.600
Bro, that’s fierce.

366
30:05.800 --> 30:08.200
Hey, I won’t allow that.

367
30:08.200 --> 30:09.560
What the hell?

368
30:09.560 --> 30:12.960
-If you want to hug someone, go hug Petong. -What?

369
30:13.040 --> 30:15.240
Go hug Petong. Stop it.

370
30:15.280 --> 30:20.920
What? No, stop it.

371
30:20.920 --> 30:22.040
No.

372
30:22.200 --> 30:26.600
I’ve always considered you a friend.

373
30:26.760 --> 30:30.040
I know. My friend, Chun.

374
30:30.040 --> 30:33.800
My bestie. My ride or die.

375
30:34.080 --> 30:37.680
Wow. “My ride or die”, he said?

376
30:40.720 --> 30:42.040
They’re in love.

377
30:46.080 --> 30:50.800
Are you still sad seeing these kids graduate?

378
30:54.040 --> 30:57.080
Well…I am a little.

379
30:58.040 --> 31:00.400
But this year, I feel a bit better.

380
31:01.240 --> 31:01.840
How?

381
31:03.200 --> 31:06.240
It’s because…

382
31:08.400 --> 31:09.920
you’re not leaving with them.

383
31:16.320 --> 31:17.280
I mean…

384
31:17.840 --> 31:21.520
You can keep me company so I won’t get lonely.

385
31:23.720 --> 31:25.080
You’re all talk.

386
31:25.960 --> 31:28.240
You’d better not leave me and go date someone.

387
31:30.920 --> 31:31.520
Why?

388
31:32.360 --> 31:34.960
Why can’t I date someone?

389
31:38.320 --> 31:39.360
No reason.

390
31:41.480 --> 31:42.760
I just won’t allow it.

391
31:47.760 --> 31:48.560
Hey, wait.

392
31:50.440 --> 31:51.680
You idiot.

393
31:53.560 --> 31:57.520
-That’s crazy. -Oh, hell no. Hell no.

394
31:57.520 --> 31:59.040
Hey, girl.

395
32:03.720 --> 32:05.000
Wait, hold on.

396
32:08.200 --> 32:09.360
You should bring one more luggage.

397
32:09.800 --> 32:14.200
No, I won’t. I’ve got too much stuff already.

398
32:16.360 --> 32:17.840
But there’s still room for you to get in.

399
32:18.360 --> 32:19.840
Wanna come with me?

400
32:23.640 --> 32:24.680
Funny.

401
32:27.800 --> 32:30.480
Try sitting on it. That might work.

402
32:33.120 --> 32:33.960
Damn.

403
32:36.360 --> 32:38.800
-There. Close it. -Yes.

404
32:40.080 --> 32:40.960
Finally.

405
32:43.000 --> 32:46.480
Took you long enough. Shouldn’t have spent your time playing games.

406
32:47.160 --> 32:48.120
Before I leave,

407
32:48.880 --> 32:50.880
let’s review our deal one more time.

408
32:53.200 --> 32:56.800
-Well…we’ll text each other every day. -Mmm.

409
32:57.160 --> 33:00.240
If there’s a problem or misunderstanding,

410
33:00.880 --> 33:02.080
we’ll talk it out right away.

411
33:02.840 --> 33:03.640
That’s right.

412
33:04.160 --> 33:04.880
What about Sundays?

413
33:05.080 --> 33:06.120
Video calls.

414
33:06.840 --> 33:10.320
I’ve put you on my schedule for the next three years.

415
33:10.440 --> 33:12.000
Good boy.

416
33:13.000 --> 33:14.280
What if someone hits on you?

417
33:16.160 --> 33:18.240
If someone hits on me,

418
33:22.040 --> 33:26.600
-I’ll feed them to the crocodile. -Good boy.

419
33:28.480 --> 33:30.600
You should stop teaching me to be weird like you.

420
33:30.640 --> 33:31.440
I can’t.

421
33:32.160 --> 33:34.000
I don’t want you to be cute with other people.

422
33:34.240 --> 33:36.480
I had to teach you to be a little weird, okay?

423
33:37.320 --> 33:39.680
My tofu.

424
33:39.800 --> 33:40.600
Oww.

425
33:43.520 --> 33:44.640
Let’s go now.

426
33:46.080 --> 33:48.880
Ready? One…two…three.

427
33:55.280 --> 33:57.080
I know I’ll miss you so much.

428
34:09.200 --> 34:11.200
I know I’ll miss you more.

429
34:43.200 --> 34:45.720
♪ Ever since that day ♪

430
34:46.640 --> 34:52.360
♪ When you and I happened to meet, it’s like a dream ♪

431
34:52.400 --> 34:53.880
♪ ’Cause you’re the one ♪

432
34:53.880 --> 34:57.480
♪ Who came along and made my heart skip a beat ♪

433
34:57.840 --> 35:04.680
♪ It feels like I’ve finally found love ♪

434
35:07.960 --> 35:11.480
1 YEAR LATER

435
35:18.000 --> 35:21.640
That’s all. Drive safely.

436
35:28.560 --> 35:31.960
-2 boxes of Hawaiian pizza. Thank you so much. -Yes.

437
35:34.040 --> 35:35.600
Hey, Bee!

438
35:35.880 --> 35:37.600
Don’t you know how to manage your shop?

439
35:37.720 --> 35:38.480
SAMING PHON FAI Look.

440
35:38.720 --> 35:41.240
Your customers are standing on the street.

441
35:41.360 --> 35:43.080
What, Chun?

442
35:43.200 --> 35:45.960
You’re jealous of me already?

443
35:45.960 --> 35:46.960
Why would I be?

444
35:46.960 --> 35:48.040
I got lots of customers, too.

445
35:48.040 --> 35:48.800
Where?

446
35:49.000 --> 35:50.600
I can only count like 10 people.

447
35:50.720 --> 35:52.120
-Yeah? -Yeah.

448
35:52.160 --> 35:53.400
Are you freaking blind?

449
35:53.400 --> 35:56.120
See how long my line is?

450
35:56.160 --> 35:57.560
I got online orders, too.

451
35:57.560 --> 36:00.360
-What’s wrong? Why are you standing like that? -Pa, enough.

452
36:01.160 --> 36:02.240
-Pa. -What?

453
36:02.400 --> 36:04.280
Your customers are hangry.

454
36:04.280 --> 36:06.880
-Damn. -For my customers’ sake.

455
36:06.880 --> 36:09.560
You’re gonna lose your customers because you’re so cocky.

456
36:09.560 --> 36:11.640
What? What does that even mean?

457
36:11.800 --> 36:15.480
-I have a business to run. -Yeah, I have a business to run, too.

458
36:15.520 --> 36:17.200
Please, come in. This way.

459
36:32.400 --> 36:32.840
Sun!

460
36:54.560 --> 36:55.160
Hey!

461
36:55.800 --> 36:56.560
Bay!

462
36:57.440 --> 36:58.400
Damn.

463
36:59.160 --> 37:00.120
You beat me again.

464
37:01.760 --> 37:02.920
What are you doing here?

465
37:03.720 --> 37:05.160
Why didn’t you tell me you were coming?

466
37:05.440 --> 37:07.000
I wanted to surprise you.

467
37:07.800 --> 37:09.360
You’re going to give a speech.

468
37:09.520 --> 37:10.800
How could I miss it?

469
37:11.200 --> 37:12.960
-No way. -Why?

470
37:13.200 --> 37:14.800
You came back just watch me give a speech?

471
37:15.480 --> 37:17.520
Fine, I’ll tell you the truth.

472
37:18.360 --> 37:19.280
My university is on break.

473
37:20.120 --> 37:21.480
So I’ll stay here for a month.

474
37:24.880 --> 37:25.680
Are you serious?

475
37:26.480 --> 37:27.160
Of course.

476
37:29.520 --> 37:31.000
Why didn’t you tell me first?

477
37:33.760 --> 37:34.960
Do you miss me that much?

478
37:35.680 --> 37:36.640
Of course I do.

479
37:37.680 --> 37:39.080
I haven’t seen you for so long.

480
37:39.560 --> 37:40.720
When we talked on the phone,

481
37:41.120 --> 37:42.560
you always acted tough.

482
37:43.240 --> 37:47.000
Seeing how much you miss me, I’m relieved.

483
37:47.560 --> 37:49.200
My tofu.

484
37:49.520 --> 37:52.440
Hey, Bay, you can’t pinch my cheek in public.

485
37:52.560 --> 37:55.480
I’m a national athlete now.

486
37:55.640 --> 37:56.720
What if someone sees me?

487
37:57.480 --> 37:59.320
-See? -Mmm.

488
37:59.400 --> 38:00.640
See this flag?

489
38:00.640 --> 38:02.920
Fine. I’ll stop doing that.

490
38:04.120 --> 38:06.800
Pinching my cheek like that… I’m embarrassed.

491
38:08.560 --> 38:09.120
Hey!

492
38:12.440 --> 38:14.320
Did you just kiss my cheek?

493
38:14.680 --> 38:15.440
You’re shy?

494
38:20.560 --> 38:21.040
A little bit.

495
38:22.760 --> 38:23.640
And do you like it?

496
38:32.400 --> 38:32.880
Yes.

497
38:41.080 --> 38:41.960
Come on. Let’s go to school.

498
38:42.520 --> 38:44.040
You’re shy, huh?

499
38:45.680 --> 38:46.240
What?

500
38:47.440 --> 38:51.000
Next, I’d like to invite one of our alumni to come up and give a speech.

501
38:57.960 --> 39:00.640
Good morning, everyone. My name’s Sun.

502
39:00.840 --> 39:02.000
I’m an alumnus of this school.

503
39:02.520 --> 39:05.840
How are you feeling on the last day of your high school life?

504
39:06.120 --> 39:06.920
Are you glad?

505
39:07.800 --> 39:10.480
Or are you worried about something?

506
39:10.480 --> 39:11.560
I’m so glad.

507
39:11.560 --> 39:14.200
I’m excited.

508
39:18.480 --> 39:23.800
I used to be so afraid of change and saying goodbye.

509
39:27.000 --> 39:32.240
Until I learned that every ending is also a new beginning.

510
39:33.520 --> 39:38.520
I thought being an athlete made me understand that.

511
39:39.160 --> 39:43.760
Because finishing one game means you’re starting another.

512
39:45.200 --> 39:46.280
But that wasn’t the reason.

513
39:51.440 --> 39:53.600
I realized those things weren’t scary

514
39:55.680 --> 39:57.560
when I received genuine love

515
39:59.920 --> 40:01.000
from the people in my life.

516
40:05.240 --> 40:07.480
(My son came up with the pizza dough recipe himself.)

517
40:07.560 --> 40:08.400
(It was love)

518
40:09.240 --> 40:12.600
APPLICATION FOR WITHDRAWAL FROM UNIVERSITY (that made me realize I didn’t have to be someone else to be loved.)

519
40:13.640 --> 40:15.640
I’ve got a new pizza recipe for you to try.

520
40:28.920 --> 40:31.040
YOU ARE CORDIALLY INVITED TO CELEBRATE OUR WEDDING

521
40:31.280 --> 40:34.840
(Love that will never change even when we do.)

522
40:37.000 --> 40:38.840
I like the tennis term ‘love-all’.

523
40:39.440 --> 40:43.640
‘Love’ sounds a bit like the French word for zero.

524
40:45.480 --> 40:47.400
It’s used when a new game begins.

525
40:49.160 --> 40:51.400
Our lives are not so different from a tennis match.

526
40:52.040 --> 40:54.480
BUSINESS CLOSED

527
40:54.640 --> 40:56.240
(I’d like all of you to believe)

528
40:56.560 --> 40:59.480
(that every ending always has a new beginning waiting for you.)

529
41:00.600 --> 41:02.600
Hello, Sun. What are you doing?

530
41:03.000 --> 41:03.760
Taking a break.

531
41:04.160 --> 41:06.000
-Is it raining there? -(But genuine love)

532
41:06.520 --> 41:10.840
-Yeah, it’s just started to drizzle. -(makes the journey to your new beginning less scary.)

533
41:11.920 --> 41:14.080
And when your new match begins,

534
41:15.360 --> 41:17.400
shout, “Love-all” and start to play.

535
41:29.280 --> 41:31.280
HE WAS RAISED WELL, HIS PASSION SHINES BRIGHT, FACE CARD NEVER DECLINED, OMG, GREAT SPEECH!

536
41:38.600 --> 41:39.800
Sun’s speech was inspiring.

537
41:40.640 --> 41:41.360
I know, right?

538
41:41.840 --> 41:44.080
It made me feel like

539
41:44.480 --> 41:47.040
I want to tell my crush I like him and get it over with.

540
41:47.880 --> 41:51.320
So I can have my new beginning, too.

541
41:52.520 --> 41:56.160
You still have a crush on that guy?

542
42:00.720 --> 42:02.840
Of course.

543
42:03.920 --> 42:04.920
What can I do?

544
42:05.320 --> 42:10.080
I see him every day. Plus, he takes such good care of me.

545
42:11.840 --> 42:13.560
How could I get over him?

546
42:20.120 --> 42:20.760
Who is he?

547
42:22.120 --> 42:23.520
You’re not gonna tell me?

548
42:31.640 --> 42:32.520
You really wanna know?

549
42:35.360 --> 42:37.720
Then…come closer.

550
42:41.200 --> 42:42.200
Closer.

551
43:11.520 --> 43:12.960
I have something to tell you, too.

552
43:13.920 --> 43:14.200
Hmm?

553
43:16.080 --> 43:16.800
Come closer.

554
43:23.400 --> 43:24.240
Boat!

555
43:25.560 --> 43:26.800
We’re at school!

556
43:26.800 --> 43:28.000
Why are you yelling?

557
43:28.000 --> 43:29.680
We can’t be doing this at school.

558
43:29.680 --> 43:30.320
Can’t we?

559
43:30.600 --> 43:32.040
What if the kids saw us?

560
43:32.360 --> 43:34.560
-Free country. -Free country?!

561
43:45.800 --> 43:46.040
Uhm…

562
43:46.600 --> 43:46.840
Uhm…

563
43:47.680 --> 43:50.480
Can I borrow Sun to play tennis with us?

564
43:51.400 --> 43:53.680
I’d like to play against a national player for once.

565
43:53.880 --> 43:56.240
Right, bro. I’ve been training so hard for this day.

566
43:56.840 --> 43:58.880
Let me go. I’ll go play with these kids.

567
43:58.880 --> 44:00.400
But I’m not done with you.

568
44:00.480 --> 44:02.960
I’ll play with them for a bit.

569
44:03.840 --> 44:05.480
Why don’t you play double then?

570
44:06.080 --> 44:07.960
I’ve brought you your rackets.

571
44:13.880 --> 44:14.800
Surprise!

572
44:15.280 --> 44:16.360
-Hey! -Hey!

573
44:17.600 --> 44:19.280
-Ooh. -Wow!

574
44:19.280 --> 44:20.440
My My My.

575
44:20.440 --> 44:22.000
Not matching rackets.

576
44:22.000 --> 44:22.880
Matching rackets.

577
44:24.000 --> 44:25.000
You got these made for us.

578
44:25.240 --> 44:25.720
Mmm.

579
44:25.880 --> 44:26.520
Thank you.

580
44:27.080 --> 44:27.360
Mmm.

581
44:27.360 --> 44:28.240
It’s a heart shape.

582
44:29.000 --> 44:30.880
-Ready? Ready? -Let’s go!

583
44:30.880 --> 44:32.920
-Come on. -Let’s go.

584
44:32.960 --> 44:33.720
Come with me.

585
45:14.640 --> 45:15.880
You were far better than me today.

586
45:17.000 --> 45:18.400
Guess I have to practice the shadowing technique again.

587
45:18.720 --> 45:19.640
So I can keep up with you.

588
45:21.120 --> 45:21.680
Okay.

589
45:22.760 --> 45:23.480
I’ll coach you.

590
45:24.560 --> 45:25.560
Should we start training now?

591
45:45.640 --> 45:46.120
Hey!

592
46:10.560 --> 46:12.640
We’re still in sync.

593
46:15.120 --> 46:16.200
No need to practice.

594
46:17.480 --> 46:18.840
Who said I’m practicing?

595
46:20.760 --> 46:21.800
This is a real match.

596
46:22.520 --> 46:24.480
♪ Ever since that day ♪ Hey, you caught me off guard!

597
46:26.000 --> 46:29.160
♪ When you and I happened to meet, -What? Come on. -Stay right there.

598
46:29.160 --> 46:31.440
it’s like a dream ♪

599
46:31.760 --> 46:33.320
♪ ’Cause you’re the one ♪

600
46:33.320 --> 46:36.920
♪ Who came along and made my heart skip a beat ♪

601
46:36.960 --> 46:42.240
♪ It feels like I’ve finally found love ♪

602
46:43.680 --> 46:46.880
SUPPORTED BY THE DEPARTMENT OF CULTURAL PROMOTION, MINISTRY OF CULTURE
